
🟩 1. Feature Flag System
"To tackle the challenge of big bang releases and improve the way we migrate complex UI like calculators or forms, I built a lightweight feature flag system using React Context and localStorage.
It allows us to ship both MVP and Final versions in the same bundle, toggle visibility at runtime, and roll out gradually — without needing a full redeploy."

🟨 2. Storybook + Unit Testing Automation
"To improve component reliability and enable design-dev alignment, I set up Storybook for isolated component development, paired with automated unit tests using Jest and Testing Library.
It allows teams to document and visually test components with real data from Contentful, reducing integration bugs and improving confidence before merging."

🟦 3. AST Tools for Developer Experience
"To reduce manual code changes and enforce standards, I’ve been experimenting with AST-based tooling — like codemods to auto-update component usage or refactor props across large codebases.
This helps maintain consistency, cut down on review cycles, and streamline migrations when component APIs change."
